description:
One push to the empty `main` of the owner-created repo, then immediate protection. This item is not a PR.

1. Make a fresh clone of core at the merge commit of site-split-10, outside any BenchBox worktree.
2. Run `git filter-repo`:
   - `--path` website/, results-explorer/, landing/, docs/blog/, _blog/ and _project/design/site-inventory/;
   - `--path landing/prompts/catalog.yaml --invert-paths`;
   - `--path-glob '*.py' --path-glob '*.sh' --invert-paths`;
   - `--path-rename` results-explorer/:explorer/, docs/blog/:blog/, _blog/:drafts/ and _project/design/site-inventory/:inventory/.
3. Before pushing, verify the following and record the results in the item context:
   - `git rev-list --all --objects` lists no .py, .sh, pyproject.toml or uv.lock;
   - `gitleaks detect` on the rewritten history is clean;
   - the .git size after `git gc --aggressive --prune=now`. Stop and ask the owner if it is over 500 MB.
4. Push `main` to BenchBox-dev/benchbox-site. This is the only direct push to its main.
5. Immediately apply site-split-21 step 1: the ruleset, the github-pages environment, the Pages source and the variables.
